  "benefits_features_and_faqs": {
    "about_overview": "Standard Chartered Priority Visa Infinite Credit Card is primarily designed to offer benefits around travel and lifestyle. Cardholders can earnaccelerated reward points on international and retail spends , making it a suitable option for frequent travellers. Additionally, travel benefits like up to 24 complimentary international and 16 domestic lounge visits per year further enhance the card’s value. However, only Priority Banking customers are eligible for complimentary international lounge access, while non-Priority customers receive only the Priority Pass membership. It’s also important to note that this card is lifetime free only for Priority Banking customers , and non-Priority Banking customers have to pay both joining and annual fees. Another drawback is the high forex markup fee of 3.5% , especially considering that this card focuses on international travel. This can significantly reduce the value of accelerated rewards on international spends. Overall, this card is a suitable option if you maintain a Priority Banking relationship with the bank and want to avail decent travel benefits.",
    "highlights": [
      "5 reward points for every Rs. 100 spent internationally or on retail",
      "2 reward points for every Rs. 100 spent on other categories",
